The letters A to H represent eight organic compounds:
A: a carboxylic acid (HCOOH type structure, methanoic/formic acid drawn as H–C(=O)–O–H);
B: an alkene with a methyl branch (H₂C=C(CH₃)–CH₃ type structure with a C=C double bond);
C: CH₃CH₂CH₂COCH₃ (a ketone, pentan-2-one);
D: C₂H₆O;
E: C₂H₄;
F: 3-methylbutan-2-one;
G: a six-carbon branched alkane (drawn structurally with CH₃ branches);
H: 3-methylbutanal.
Define the term unsaturated compound.
